Fix: flaky DB-unreachable test discovered while running sbt-scoverage's coverage suite

Summary: The 'unreachable Postgres' test used postgres.mappedPort(5432) + 1 to
simulate a closed port. Under scoverage instrumentation, order-service's suite ran 3
Testcontainers Postgres instances concurrently with adjacent dynamically-assigned host
ports (e.g. 51237/38/39) — so +1 could coincide with a DIFFERENT, live container's real
port, making the 'unreachable' assumption false and the test intermittently see a 201
instead of a 5xx. Fixed by using a fixed, always-unreachable port (1, a privileged port
nothing binds to) instead of deriving one from another container's mapped port.

Files changed:
- modules/order-service/src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderServicePostgresIntegrationSuite.scala
